<https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/datasets/kbase-nmdc-arkin> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dcterms:requires <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/glossary/berdl-tenant> ;
    schema1:about <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/explanations/provenance-is-not-in-the-name> ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "draft" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema1:description "Omics records originating with NMDC, which the Arkin Lab at LBNL has extended with vector embeddings, organism trait assignments, and a reconciled annotation layer." ;
    schema1:keywords "produced-by-arkin-lab" ;
    schema1:name "kbase.nmdc_arkin" ;
    schema1:text """# Provenance
Producer: the Arkin Lab at LBNL, working from NMDC omics. Host tenant: `kbase`.
Snapshot currency 2026-05-27 as recorded by the audit.""" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/datasets/nmdc-metadata> .

<https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/datasets/kbase-nmdc-neon> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dcterms:requires <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/glossary/berdl-tenant> ;
    schema1:about <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/explanations/provenance-is-not-in-the-name> ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "draft" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema1:description "Observations collected by the NSF National Ecological Observatory Network, processed through workflows of the kind NMDC uses." ;
    schema1:keywords "produced-by-neon" ;
    schema1:name "kbase.nmdc_neon" ;
    schema1:text """# Provenance
Producer: the NSF NEON program. Host tenant: `kbase`. The `nmdc_` element of the
name refers to the processing style, which is a third thing again, distinct from both
the host and the producer.""" .

<https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/datasets/nmdc-ncbi-biosamples> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dcterms:requires <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/glossary/berdl-tenant> ;
    schema1:about <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/explanations/provenance-is-not-in-the-name> ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "draft" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema1:description "A copy of NCBI BioSample records, pulled from NCBI and hosted under the nmdc tenant so NMDC users can reach them alongside NMDC records." ;
    schema1:keywords "produced-by-ncbi" ;
    schema1:name "nmdc.ncbi_biosamples" ;
    schema1:text """# Provenance
Producer: NCBI; the authority for these records is ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample.
Host tenant: `nmdc`. This is a case where the two axes differ.""" .

<https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/datasets/nmdc-metadata> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dcterms:requires <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/glossary/berdl-tenant> ;
    schema1:about <https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/explanations/provenance-is-not-in-the-name> ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "draft" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema1:description "Study, biosample, and omics records that NMDC itself produces and treats as authoritative." ;
    schema1:keywords "produced-by-nmdc" ;
    schema1:name "nmdc.metadata" ;
    schema1:text """# Provenance
Producer: NMDC. Host tenant: `nmdc`. Both axes agree here, which is what
makes this the authoritative surface for NMDC records.""" .

<https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/explanations/provenance-is-not-in-the-name> a lokf:Explanation ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "draft" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema1:description "A database name carries one axis, where the data is hosted. Who produced the data is a second, independent axis, and no naming scheme carries both at once." ;
    schema1:genre "explanation" ;
    schema1:keywords "berdl",
        "modelling",
        "provenance" ;
    schema1:name "Provenance is not in the name" ;
    schema1:text """# The two axes
A BERDL database name gives you a tenant and a short label. The tenant says who hosts and
curates the database. It does not say who produced the records inside it, and it was never
meant to.

Those two facts vary independently. A tenant can host data it did not produce, and data a
group produced can be hosted by someone else. Two independent axes cannot both be encoded in
one string without losing information, so a reader who infers a producer from a name is
inferring something the name does not carry.

# Why this is the right shape for a graph
Hosting and production are separate properties of the same resource, which is exactly what a
graph represents well and a naming convention does not. `prov:wasDerivedFrom` states the
production lineage; the tenant stays where it belongs, in the name and the catalog.

The tenant boundaries here are deliberate. NMDC-derived products were placed in the `kbase`
tenant so that the `nmdc` tenant stays a clean, authoritative surface that the NMDC team
curates. That separation is what makes the hosting axis meaningful. This bundle adds the
production axis alongside it rather than in place of it.""" .

<https://w3id.org/turbomam/nmdc-lokf-demo/glossary/berdl-tenant> a schema1:DefinedTerm ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "draft" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema1:name "BERDL tenant" ;
    schema1:text """# Note
A tenant says where a database is hosted. It does not say who produced the data.""" ;
    skos:definition "The top-level namespace of a database in the BERDL lakehouse catalog, such as nmdc, kbase, globalusers, or a username." .

